---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="About" description="About DnR Dispatch Research — independent market research on US equities, macro, and strategy.">
  <div class="shell">
    <header class="page-header">
      <p class="page-header__eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>About DnR Dispatch Research</h1>
    </header>
    <div class="static-prose">
      <p>
        DnR Dispatch Research is an independent research publication covering US equities, macro,
        and strategy. It runs on two formats: <strong>The Brief</strong>, short wire-style dispatches
        filed when something moves — a print, a Fed decision, a guidance change — and longer analytical
        notes under Strategy Notes and Earnings Watch, where the goal is to work through the reasoning
        behind a view rather than just report the headline.
      </p>
      <p>
        It's edited independently of any brokerage, asset manager, or listed company it may
        write about.
      </p>

      <h2>Editorial approach</h2>
      <p>
        Dispatches lead with the fact, not the take — what happened, who said it, and why it matters
        to positioning, written to be read in under a minute. Strategy Notes take the opposite shape:
        one idea, argued in full, with the reasoning shown rather than just the conclusion.
      </p>
      <p>
        Every piece is written by the same desk, so a reader building a mental model of how we think
        can do that over time — the same discipline that makes single-analyst research worth
        following in the first place.
      </p>

      <h2>About the author</h2>
      <p>
        DnR Dispatch Research was built to give US equity market practitioners news that's
        current and easy to understand. It's part of the DnR Group, founded by
        <strong>Dimas Adi Darmawan</strong> — a US equities market practitioner of four years —
        with an approach that draws on macroeconomics, company earnings, geopolitics, and other
        perspectives shaping price action.
      </p>

      <h2>Get in touch</h2>
      <p>
        For corrections, tips, or licensing questions, reach the desk through the subscribe link
        in the footer — a direct contact address will be added here once set up.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
